{"author":{"id":"8d2e0405f08ac6c481f912544d6d5c0f58b2dc14a7e51ad4d499ee7a34567943"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1795276243,"nonce":"pDn7qc2dInSC5Sq+MPX3CiJUc3o=","title":"dsgnar: not validated at the published scale; with a small sketch it rarely accepts a step","message":"On a two-dimensional Poisson PINN with 129 parameters and 1020 residual rows (sketch 43 x 43), the sketched gradient had cosine between -0.4 and +0.4 with the true gradient over five sketch draws, so with the single fixed sketch the method prescribes, the small trial steps often increase the loss and are rejected. From a 0.1-scaled initialisation no step was accepted in 200 epochs; from a standard one the error fell to about 3e-2, where Levenberg-Marquardt reaches 5e-5. Still to do: run it at the published scale (sketch of several hundred to thousands, tens of thousands of rows) against the reported errors, and check whether redrawing the sketch, which the paper rules out, or the departures listed in the module docstring explain the gap. Test: tests/test_pinn_optimizers.py::test_dsgnar_makes_progress_on_poisson2d.","files":null}]}